WEBVTT

00:00:03.581 --> 00:00:12.151
Revenue Ledger
One ledger of the revenue every Genesis entity earns: credited to the RM and any referrer, and reconciled to the finance figures.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.840
Most revenue lines are posted by the business that earns them
An FX deal, a paid advisory fee invoice…

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.160
Sign in as Deepak Mungur — Forex Dealer
Forex dealer — books client deals

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:33.280
Rodrigues Seafood Exports Ltd sells USD 50,000 of export proceeds
Booked at 47.61 — a quarter of a rupee under today's mid rate

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:41.360
Saved: the deal works out its spread over the mid rate
That spread is the desk's income — and it is posted to the Revenue Ledger

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.520
Growth ▸ Revenue: every fee and income line, by entity, type and month
Finance and the Head of BD post and reconcile it

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.840
Sign in as Shalini Ramtohul — Head of BD & Strategic Partnerships
Head of BD — posts and reconciles revenue

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.560
One line per client, product and month — with its source and reconciliation status
Monthly summaries come from the loan system, the funds and the brokerage

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:01.280
Further right: the amount in rupees, the source and the reconciliation status
Every column can be sorted

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:17.440
The line the dealer's deal just posted
Source: FX deal (automatic)

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:30.320
A commercial facility for Moka Textiles Ltd has been arranged
The arrangement fee is posted by hand: Revenue ▸ New Revenue

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:38.280
Bruno Chan manages the client; Priya Ramdin referred the deal
Credit is split: 25% to the referring RM

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:51.360
The fee is converted to rupees and the credit split automatically
MUR 318,750 to Bruno Chan · MUR 106,250 to Priya Ramdin

00:01:51.360 --> 00:02:03.480
Month end: enter the figure booked in the accounting system
Reconciliation: Awaiting finance figure

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:09.400
Accounting booked MUR 420,000 — a variance of MUR 5,000
Reconciliation: Variance to investigate

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:19.000
Finance finds the missing MUR 5,000 posting and corrects its figure
Edit the line again

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.280
Ledger and accounts agree
Reconciliation: Reconciled

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:31.680
Narrow the ledger by entity, type and month
Type any words from the columns — every word must match

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:42.280
Lending · arrangement fees · 2026-10
The count shows how many lines match

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:50.400
Forex · 2026-10: the desk's monthly summary and the deals posted automatically
Entity names, revenue types and months all work

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.880
Export gives the lines shown as a spreadsheet
For incentive calculations — with names and labels, not codes

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.880
The ledger feeds the management dashboards
Group Executive and RM League Table

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:05.680
Sign in as Anjali Gopee — Chief Operating Officer
Chief Operating Officer — reads group revenue

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:12.280
Group Executive: revenue by entity and by month
Lending leads; Forex includes today's deal

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:18.440
Next: the RM League Table
Pick it from the dashboard menu

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:24.581
RM League Table: the revenue each RM is credited with
Referring RMs get their split in the next chart

00:03:24.581 --> 00:03:32.080
Summary
Revenue is posted where it is earned, credited fairly and reconciled before anyone reports on it.
